<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 2.03 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 2.03 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4565 to the dollar, up from 3.4680 on Monday and at 1.9045 to the mark, up from 1.9320, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.03 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Monday's fix at -2.90 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
